<title>USA: USDA raises Russia GSM-102 credit line by $20 mln.</title>
<headline>USDA raises Russia GSM-102 credit line by $20 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday said it boosted Russia's GSM-102 credit guarantee line by $20 million to $50 million for fiscal year 1997.</p>
<p>A USDA official said Wednesday the department was studying boosting the dwindling credit line as a means to help Russia buy U.S. wheat. Earlier this week, Russian Agriculture Minister Viktor Khlystun said Russia would import up to three million tonnes of high-quality wheat in 1997.</p>
</text>
